# tally 2.3.1 S9 (L §3.1 `never`: ordering against it is allowed, `min`, `max`, `argmin` and `argmax`
# included; arithmetic is refused): min(never, d) is d (m1), max never (m2), and so over a binding (m3 to m6);
# add_days refuses it (m8). Before: m1 to m6 RUN-DOMAIN `never and <d> compared`.
=== never.tally
model nev
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
index ks = [a, b]
input dl[k in ks]: date
input d: date
input nv: date

ask m1: min(nv, d)
ask m2: max(nv, d)
ask m3: min(dl[k] for k in ks)
ask m4: max(dl[k] for k in ks)
ask m5: argmin(dl[k] for k in ks)
ask m6: argmax(dl[k] for k in ks)
ask m7: d < nv
ask m8: add_days(nv, 1)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dl[a] = 2026-03-01 "s"
  dl[b] = never "s"
  d = 2026-05-01 "s"
  nv = never "s"
=== expect
m1: 2026-05-01
  cut 2026-06-30
m2: never
  cut 2026-06-30
m3: 2026-03-01
  cut 2026-06-30
m4: never
  cut 2026-06-30
m5: a
  cut 2026-06-30
m6: b
  cut 2026-06-30
m7: true
  cut 2026-06-30
m8: refused: RUN-NONE never in add_days
  cut 2026-06-30
